skill: "collections-dunning-automation"
sections[3]:
  - "# collections-dunning-automation\n\nOperate the collections ladder from gentle reminder to bad-debt provision. Use when AR ages past 60 days, when a dunning stage fires, or when provisioning is due for the quarter. Excludes disputed invoices until the dispute closes, and hands legal-grade escalations to the operator for a human decision.\n\nOwner: role-accounts-manager (pod-gna, finance). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"ar-aging.toon 61-90 and 90+ slices; disputes.toon (exclusions); payment history per customer; dunning policy dunning-policy.toon (stage schedule, channels, provisions)\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/finance/dunning-schedule.toon with per-customer stage, next action and due date; provision-schedule.toon; effectiveness metrics\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load dunning-policy.toon and record its version; the ladder, channels and provision rates all come from policy, not from this run's judgment.\n2. Build the working set from the 61-90 and 90+ slices; remove disputed invoices per disputes.toon and list the exclusions so silence is explainable.\n3. Assign each customer its current stage from payment history: reminder (day 3 past due), formal notice (day 10), escalation review (day 30), handoff review (day 60), provision review (day 120).\n4. Align automated reminders with the billing stack: where stripe-automation already sends payment emails, the ladder adds actions, not duplicate sends.\n5. Compute per-stage actions and due dates with run_command; stage advancement is arithmetic on the policy schedule, never discretionary.\n6. At escalation review, assemble the account evidence (aging history, promises, contact log) and emit ask_question naming whether to continue dunning or route to the operator for a commercial decision.\n7. At provision review, apply the policy provision rate to the uncollected balance and write provision-schedule.toon for role-cfo's review.\n8. Track effectiveness per stage (collection rate after stage, days-to-pay delta) and write it into dunning-schedule.toon; stages that never collect get flagged for policy review with the numbers attached.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nprovisions to role-cfo; legal-grade escalations to operator; policy findings to dunning-policy owner.\n"
